WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.160
After the prizes were given out, it was time to eat them.

2
00:00:07.161 --> 00:00:13.961
Alice did not eat her thimble, of course, but the other creatures ate their candy.

3
00:00:13.962 --> 00:00:20.386
The large birds complained that the candy was so small, they couldn't taste it.

4
00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:28.745
The small birds coughed and choked on their candy because it was so large.

5
00:00:28.746 --> 00:00:32.386
But after a while everyone settled down.

6
00:00:32.387 --> 00:00:38.195
The creatures sat in a circle and begged the Mouse to tell them his story.

7
00:00:38.196 --> 00:00:42.018
"You promised to tell me about your family," Alice said.

8
00:00:42.019 --> 00:00:45.389
"And why you hate C and D

9
00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:48.349
." She didn't say "cats and dogs."

10
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:52.156
She didn't want to upset the Mouse again.

11
00:00:52.157 --> 00:00:57.715
"Mine is a long and sad tale," the Mouse began.

12
00:00:57.716 --> 00:01:00.571
Alice studied the mouse's body.

13
00:01:00.572 --> 00:01:06.319
"You definitely have a long tail, but I don't understand why it's sad."

14
00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:10.744
"No, not my tail ," the Mouse said

15
00:01:10.745 --> 00:01:16.688
impatiently. "My tale , as

16
00:01:16.689 --> 00:01:21.017
in story." He went

17
00:01:21.018 --> 00:01:28.093
on talking. Meanwhile Alice kept thinking about words that sound alike but have

18
00:01:28.094 --> 00:01:34.273
different meanings. "Now do you understand why I don't like cats?" the Mouse said

19
00:01:34.274 --> 00:01:37.675
to Alice. "What?" Alice looked at him

20
00:01:37.676 --> 00:01:42.138
and blinked. "You weren't paying attention!" the Mouse

21
00:01:42.139 --> 00:01:45.807
said angrily. "I don't know why I bothered telling you

22
00:01:45.808 --> 00:01:48.614
this story." He started to

23
00:01:48.615 --> 00:01:54.781
walk away. Alice felt bad that she had upset

24
00:01:54.782 --> 00:01:59.532
him again. "Please come back and repeat your story!" she called

25
00:01:59.533 --> 00:02:02.950
after him. "I promise to listen to every word

26
00:02:02.951 --> 00:02:08.618
this time." "Yes, please do come back," all the others

27
00:02:08.619 --> 00:02:14.628
said together. But the Mouse only shook his head impatiently and

28
00:02:14.629 --> 00:02:20.605
walked faster. "What a pity he wouldn't stay." The

29
00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:23.565
Parrot sighed. "I wish Dinah was here,"

30
00:02:23.566 --> 00:02:26.347
Alice said. "She would fetch him

31
00:02:26.348 --> 00:02:31.848
for us." "And who is Dinah, if I may ask?" the Parrot

32
00:02:31.849 --> 00:02:35.885
said. "Dinah's my cat. She's so good at catching

33
00:02:35.886 --> 00:02:42.318
mice." Alice replied eagerly, for she was always happy to talk about her

34
00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:46.587
pet. "And you should see her chasing

35
00:02:46.588 --> 00:02:53.154
birds!" All the birds started talking at once, and some hurried away as fast as they

36
00:02:53.155 --> 00:02:58.132
could. One old magpie began wrapping himself in a

37
00:02:58.133 --> 00:03:06.890
scarf. "I really must be going. This air is bad for my

38
00:03:06.891 --> 00:03:12.472
throat!" A canary called out in a trembling voice to her children, "Come away, my

39
00:03:12.473 --> 00:03:21.104
dears. It's time for us to go

40
00:03:21.105 --> 00:03:25.043
home." Alice was soon left all

41
00:03:25.044 --> 00:03:29.314
alone. "I wish I'd never mentioned Dinah," she said

42
00:03:29.315 --> 00:03:35.595
sadly. "Nobody seems to like her down here, but I think she's the best cat in the

43
00:03:35.596 --> 00:03:41.177
world. Oh, Dinah! I wonder if I'll ever see you

44
00:03:41.178 --> 00:03:47.106
again!" Poor Alice began to cry because she felt so lonely and

45
00:03:47.107 --> 00:03:50.880
sad. In a little while, however, she heard

46
00:03:50.881 --> 00:03:56.541
footsteps. She looked up eagerly, hoping that the Mouse had changed his mind and was coming

47
00:03:56.542 --> 00:04:00.057
back. But once again it was the White

48
00:04:00.058 --> 00:04:07.551
Rabbit. This time he was walking slowly and looking anxiously about, as if he'd lost

49
00:04:07.552 --> 00:04:10.866
something. Alice heard him muttering to himself.

50
00:04:10.867 --> 00:04:21.194
"The Duchess! The Duchess!" the White Rabbit said as he looked high and low.

51
00:04:21.195 --> 00:04:25.662
"Oh, my paws! Oh, my fur and whiskers!

52
00:04:25.663 --> 00:04:29.945
The Duchess is going to be so angry if I'm late!

53
00:04:29.946 --> 00:04:32.747
I wonder where I could have dropped them.

54
00:04:32.748 --> 00:04:35.826
I don't see them anywhere!"

55
00:04:35.827 --> 00:04:42.137
Alice guessed right away that he was looking for his gloves and fan.

56
00:04:42.138 --> 00:04:47.334
She happily began hunting for them, but they were nowhere to be seen.

57
00:04:47.335 --> 00:04:50.837
In fact, everything had changed.

58
00:04:50.838 --> 00:04:54.258
She seemed to be outdoors now.

59
00:04:54.259 --> 00:05:03.130
The great hall with the glass table and little door had disappeared.

